body: "## Current-head hosted evidence (not a product assertion failure)\n\nPR #291 remains at `7a3fffd937ad47a54fb9aecc9bff42e537b2036d` when rechecked 2026-10-27 17:46 UTC. Its [lifecycle job](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40535669186/job/122300112202) failed at 16:42 UTC before the first linked lifecycle model executed. The dependent `test` job is skipped, not passing.\n\nThe retained log reports:\n\n- `failure_category: trust_refusal`\n- `source_ref=feat/append-only-release-corrections, current_ref=unknown`\n- `testing.allow_untrusted_linked_tests=true` is required in addition to the supplied CLI flag, or the current commands must be explicitly acknowledged.\n- `assertion_failure: 0`, `recorded: false`, and `trusted: false`.\n\nThe [exact workflow](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/blob/7a3fffd937ad47a54fb9aecc9bff42e537b2036d/.github/workflows/ci.yml) creates a fresh temporary HOME and invokes:\n`node node_modules/@unbrained/pm-cli/dist/cli.js test pmc-release-corrections --run --only-last --progress --allow-untrusted-linked-tests --timeout 1200`.\nIt does not establish the required linked-command trust in that isolated CI context first. The following linked command, behavioral revert proof, packed acceptance checks and full dependent gates therefore do not run.\n\n## Expected / actual and impact\n\nThe [canonical release-corrections item](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/blob/7a3fffd937ad47a54fb9aecc9bff42e537b2036d/.agents/pm/features/pmc-release-corrections.toon) requires the focused lifecycle/revert/packed evidence before full Node22/26 npm/Bun gates, preserving truthful exact-head verification and prior thresholds. Expected: reviewed CI commands execute under an explicitly established, narrowly scoped trust contract. Actual: the required gate stops at trust admission, leaving current-head model and release evidence incomplete.\n\nThis is a CI setup blocker supported by hosted logs and static source, not a locally reproduced runtime defect, failed lifecycle assertion, or evidence that released consumers are broken. The trust refusal itself is correct fail-closed behavior.\n\n## Acceptance / regression criteria\n\n- Establish explicit trust for the reviewed linked commands in the disposable CI context using the supported SDK/CLI trust mechanism, without weakening user/default trust policy or inheriting credentials.\n- Cover the fresh-HOME, detached/unknown-ref CI case and retain refusal for genuinely unacknowledged foreign commands.\n- Re-run the exact new head: both linked checks, behavioral revert proofs, fixed models, packed checks and dependent Node22/26 npm/Bun gates. Record actual counts and links, not queued/past-head results.\n- Preserve existing coverage thresholds, assertions, environment isolation and truthful incomplete status until these gates execute.\n\nDeduplication: all 293 all-status issue/PR records, current PR conversation/inline comments and the canonical feature record checked. No dedicated equivalent trust-admission CI blocker found. PR #291 remains the implementation owner. No settings, source, provider state or trust configuration was modified during this review.\n\n---\n\n### GitHub comments (3)\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-28T17:01:10Z)\n>\n> Canonical PM lineage: [pmc-release-corrections](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/blob/feat/append-only-release-corrections/.agents/pm/features/pmc-release-corrections.toon), carried by PR #291. The linked trust-admission evidence and required lifecycle verification belong to that delivery.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-10-28T17:01:40Z)\n>\n> ## Current-head reconciliation: trust admission fixed; a separate fixture blocker remains\n> \n> At PR #291 head `df161e7a4039849cf8ec0a31017e30184fb9a5db`, [lifecycle job 122949700580](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/actions/runs/40726109410/job/122949700580) now executes the linked lifecycle command. Its final receipt reports `trust_refusal: 0`, so the original trust-admission failure is superseded for this head.\n> \n> The omitted/filtered-capture case and the 500-seeded-native-lifecycle model pass. The third case, “the producer's empty-title filter cannot reserve a later published claim,” fails when the SDK refuses a repeat closure of already-terminal `life-empty`. The linked command returns exit 1 after 454463 ms; dependent full test jobs remain skipped, not successful. This is hosted test-fixture evidence, not a released-runtime or data-loss claim.\n> \n> The existing canonical [pmc-lifecycle-repeat-closure](https://github.com/unbraind/pm-changelog/blob/df161e7a4039849cf8ec0a31017e30184fb9a5db/.agents/pm/issues/pmc-lifecycle-repeat-closure.toon) already owns that follow-up. It explicitly requires supported reopen/update transitions without disabling the terminal guard or weakening ownership, immutability and correction assertions. No duplicate issue is needed.\n> \n> Acceptance: preserve the successful narrow CI trust contract and foreign-command refusal; repair the fixture through supported SDK lifecycle transitions; rerun the exact updated head's lifecycle cases, behavioral proofs, packed acceptance and dependent gates. Local full-suite execution was not performed during this review.\n\n> **@unbraind** (2026-11-02T09:26:26Z)\n>\n> Fixed on main. Evidence: PR #291 merged 2026-10-28T18:06Z with the trust admission established (lifecycle job 122949700580 reports trust_refusal: 0 at head df161e7); main CI success run 41220085603 (2026-10-31T16:31Z) (Found in the 2026-11-02 triage of issues the blind issue watch missed.)"
